<title>FINLAND: Kemira extends losses on profit warning.</title>
<headline>Kemira extends losses on profit warning.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Finnish state-controlled chemicals group Kemira Oy continued to slide in lively trade on Thursday afternoon depressed by a profit warning released on Tuesday, brokers said.</p>
<p>At 1520/1220 GMT, Kemira traded at a two-week low 47.50, down 1.50 markka or some three percent. Trade was a lively 14 million markka.</p>
<p>There were mainly foreign investors selling Kemira, brokers said. &quot;Some big foreign investors have drawn their conclusions from the profit warning,&quot; one broker said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-0-6805 0248</p>
